Check for pricing and availability&nbsp;online for <a href="https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/234245">Gooseberry Administrative Site at Recreation.gov</a> or by telephone at&nbsp;877-444-6777. This site does not honor America the Beautiful passes.<br />
<br />
Gooseberry Admin Site Cabins are managed by the Fishlake National Forest.&nbsp;Phone: 435-896-9233.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Overnight Use: 1 - 100 people - $175 per night.<br />
Overnight Use hours: 2:00 PM -11:00 AM. Max of 100 people. Day Use: 1 - 100 people - $100/ day.<br />
Day Use hours: 6:00 AM - 10:00 PM. Max of 100 people. Reservations only, and fee must reach the office in Willows, CA&nbsp;no later than 7 business days after initial reservation request to guarantee the reservation. Cash, check or money order only, made payable to US FOREST SERVICE. There is a $20 cancellation fee. Interagency Passes do not apply to group campgrounds. If canceled 20&nbsp;days or less from date of arrival, this will result in the loss of the first day&#39;s fee, any remaining fees are refundable.&nbsp;

The Forest Service operates the Sourgrass Recreation Area and charges the following fees: 

Campsite fee prices, 2024 &amp; 2025 $30&nbsp;per night and fee raises to $35&nbsp;per night in 2026. &nbsp; 

Sourgrass Day Use fee is $5 per group per vehicle.&nbsp; 

The America the Beautiful, Interagency Senior and Access Passes are honored and receive 50% off the nightly rate. Only applicable to the single site the pass holder occupies. 

&nbsp;Pass number must be written on fee envelope.&nbsp; 

The Interagency Annual, Senior, Military, 4th Grade&nbsp;and Volunteer passes do provide free day at the Sourgrass Day Use Area.&nbsp; 

No dispersed camping within the Recreation Area.&nbsp;

$30.00 ($33.30)* per night, single site<br />
$60.00 ($66.60)* &nbsp;per night, double site<br />
